!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
! Cross-section data for iproc = [23] : H2O2+hv->OH+OH : T dep.
! Source : JPL-2006 (table 4-9, p. 4-19).
! http://www.atmosphere.mpg.de/enid/2295
! -> Catalogue -> "Peroxides" -> "H2O2" -> "JPL-2002"
! Rem1: qy = 1.0 only for wl > 230 nm as recommended by JPL-2011 (p.257,259)
!       for shorter wavelengths, qy=0.85 i.e. we assume new branch ->HO2+H 
!       (not mentioned by JPL-2006) is for all wl<230 nm
! Rem2: Temperature influence:
!    i) 190-260nm: T indep.
!   ii) 260-350nm: T dep. according to the formula:
!           1.e21 * crs = chi sum An*wl^n + (1-chi)*sum Bn*wl^n
!       where chi= (1+exp(-1265/T))**-1 and
!       An and Bn are parameters introduced in CRS_CFC.
!       The cross sections are computed in subroutine CRS_TDEP.
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :        55  | Finishes at wl interval :  102
